WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.518
The core contribution is SKiNN, the Stellar
Kinematics Neural Network.

00:00:04.598 --> 00:00:09.116
It is the first time the strategy of replacing an
expensive model component with a neural

00:00:09.196 --> 00:00:13.713
network has been applied to the kinematic-modeling
aspect of gravitational lens modeling.

00:00:13.793 --> 00:00:18.311
Crucially,

00:00:18.391 --> 00:00:22.909
SKiNN emulates only the JAM physics calculation
rather than being applied directly to observations.

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:27.507
This design choice keeps the physics of the overall
model intact while exploiting the

00:00:27.587 --> 00:00:32.104
speed and versatility of neural networks.

00:00:32.184 --> 00:00:36.702
The result is a roughly 300-fold speedup at
sub-percent accuracy,

00:00:36.782 --> 00:00:41.300
which finally makes joint lensing plus kinematics
modeling computationally feasible.
